:seac
#SEaC: Approximately Complete Operating System

It is a 32-bit, monolithic, preemptive multitasking operating system. A main task handles ~TECOP~ management, interprets ~commands~ sent to the system, updates the screen, and performs periodic tasks (floppy drive management, etc.). Other tasks are created when executing a command associated with an executable file. To switch between applications (when an application requires an interface), use the Alt+Tab keys.
The system uses a ~log~ where each task can write the results of its operations.
:navigation
#Navigation between interfaces
Each application on SEaC occupies the entire screen; to switch between applications, hold down the Alt key and press the Tab key to cycle through the interfaces.

When ~tecop~ is displayed, you can access an interface directly by clicking the corresponding line at the top of the screen or by pressing the associated function key.
:commands:command:cmd
#commands available with the SEaC operating system:

##Built-in commands:
>~AF~/~ECHO~ displays a line of text or the contents of a file
>~EFJ~ clear system log
>~DIR~/~LS~ list the contents of a folder
>~DEF~ loads a definition file
>~SUP~/~RM~ delete a file
>~COP~ copies a file
>~REN~ rename a file
>~VER~ displays the system version
>~CD~ changes working folder
>~ND~/~MK~ create new folder
>~LD~ lists installed disks and partitions
>~LM~ displays the memory organization
>~LV~ displays supported video modes
>~LT~/~PS~ show running tasks
>~MODV~ changes the video mode
>~EFJ~ clear system log
>~FDS~ set system folder
>~MTT~ modifies the execution time of the task
>~STOP~ stop a task
>~VMEM~ read memory
>~PWR~ Arrête ou redémarre l'ordinateur
>~AFT~ change l'affichage principal
##Editors:
>~EDT~ text editor
>~EDH~ hex editor
>~EDG~ character map editor
>~PARTD~ partitioner/disk formatter
##Various:
>~FASM~ x86 assembler compiler
>~AJARCH~
>~EXPL~ file explorer
>~CALC~ calculator
>~DATE~ system clock
>~UTF8~ unicode to utf8 conversion
>~MAN~ manual
>~TERM~ serial and TCP terminal
>~LSPCI~ list installed pci devices
>~LSUSB~ list installed usb devices
>~ICS~ GUI/desktop
>~VOIR~ image file viewer
>~PILOTE~ driver manager
>~LTP~ advanced task listing
>~IFF~ donne des informations sur les fichier
##-Network usage:
>~IPCONFIG~ network card configurator
>~PING~ test connection
>~CDNS~ DNS client
>~TRACE~ trace route
>~CIRC~ IRC client
>~SNIF~ displays received frame metadata
>~SCANIP~ ip address scanner
>~CHTTP~ http client
>~CFTP~ ftp client
>~NSN~ smolnet navigator
##Servers:
>~SHTTP~ http server
>~STFTP~ tftp server
>~STLNT~ telnet remote command server
>~SPXE~ serveur DHCP avec option pxe
##Network Driver:
>~RTL8139~ ~3C90X~ ~I8254X~
:cd:cop:cp:sup:rm:ren:mc:dir:ls:nd:mk
#Commands for file manipulation

command: _cd_    
change folder, cd.. return to parent folder

command: _dir_ (or _ls_)
Lists the contents of the folder in use

command: _sup XXX_ (or _rm XXX_)
delete the XXX file

command: _cop XXX YYY ZZZ_ (or _cp XXX YYY ZZZ_)
copy the XXX file to the YYY folder with ZZZ options
>-e overwrites existing files
>-f only copies files
>-d only copies folders
>-n creates the destination folder
>-r:NNNN renames the copied file

command: _ren XXX YYY_ (or _mv XXX YYY_)
rename XXX file to YYY

command: _ld_
list the partitions and cdrom which have been detected by the system (no argument)

command: _nd XXX_ (or _mk XXX_)
create and open new directory XXX
:lm:lt:ps:mtt:stop
#Application management commands

command: _lm_
List the memory spaces used by the system (no argument)

command: _ltp_ (or _ps_)
List Tasks running on the system 

command: _ltp_
a variant of the _LT_ command that provides more information about the tasks

command: _stop XXX_
Stop task numbers XXX

command: _mtt XXX YYY_
set the execution time of the task XXX to the value YYY (unit of time 2.5ms)

:lv:modv
#Video setting commands

command: _lv_       
List of display modes recognized by the video card

command: _modv XXX_
change the video mode of the screen to the mode
XXX = mode numbers, XXX*YYY for resolution

:efj:af:fds:ver:date:vmem
#Log Manipulation Commands

command: _efj_
Erase the contents of the system log

command: _fds_
Makes system record that the folder in use is the system folder

command: _ver_
Show system version in system log

command: _af XXX_
add XXX text or XXX file content to log

command: _date_
displays the time and date from the machine's clock

command: _vmem XXX_
displays the memory content at absolute address XXX
:aft
#AFT
change the task that is displayed

command: _aft XXX_
>>with:
>>>XXX = Task numbers to display, if absent, the ~tecop~ is displayed, and the log is forced to scroll to the end

